<p>A resize-performance fix: dragging a split divider or resizing the window
with Mirror Screen and streaming log tabs open no longer slows to a crawl.</p>
<h3>Fixes</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Resizing is smooth with logs streaming</strong> — the log view re-wrapped its
entire buffer on every tick of a drag, pinning a CPU core; it now re-wraps
once, when the drag rests. Log feeds also coalesce their updates a little
more (three refreshes per second instead of eight), which cuts idle CPU
with a busy logcat tab roughly in half.</li>
</ul>
